WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.520
Superman who? Dwayne Johnson seems poised&nbsp;
to turn the DC Universe upside-down with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.840
the release of "Black Adam" next week, at least&nbsp;
according to those who've already seen the movie.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.940
Early reviews for the Warner Bros. flick have&nbsp;
it pegged as an overwhelmingly brutal and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.920
honest take on the Black Adam character,&nbsp;
who "literally kills anyone and everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.400
in his way," per Collider's Steven&nbsp;
Weintraub. He wrote in his review:

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.880
"[Johnson]'s fantastic as Black Adam ... and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.760
I loved that he didn't pull&nbsp;
back on who Black Adam is."

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.400
For those who might not know, DC's "Black Adam"&nbsp;
seemed destined to fail in many people's eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.480
with all the woes that Warner Bros. has&nbsp;
experienced as of late. Back in March,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.500
the film was reportedly pushed back&nbsp;
from a summer release to October 21,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.580
2022, due to COVID-related production&nbsp;
delays involving its visual effects.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.240
Producer Hiram Garcia explained&nbsp;
the situation to The Wrap, saying:

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.160
"I think we're just in a world right now where&nbsp;
there was a huge and understandable freeze-up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.300
when the pandemic hit and a lot of productions&nbsp;
were put on hold. Now that the industry has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.280
really roared back, the pipeline for VFX is&nbsp;
so jammed ... and we're just in a situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.940
where the majority of the VFX houses&nbsp;
are just completely swamped with work."

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.700
With this in mind, many people feared that "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.060
Adam" was doomed to fail in the&nbsp;
eyes of critics and audiences.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.460
But according to people who got early screenings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.140
of "Black Adam," the DC film is unlike&nbsp;
any comic book movie that's come before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.240
it — with one critic even describing&nbsp;
it as a "300-style action spectacle."

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.700
Critic Paul McGuire Grimes tweeted that it was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.380
quote, "Epic on Every Level." Similarly,&nbsp;
Screen Rant's Joe Deckelmeier tweeted:

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.900
"#BlackAdam is a game-changer! [Dwayne&nbsp;
Johnson] is electrifyingly brutal as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.620
Black Adam! ... The action in&nbsp;
the film is non-stop &amp; seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:46.980
the [Justice Society of America]&nbsp;
on the big screen was a thrill!"

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.640
While it definitely looks like there are a&nbsp;
few things in the movie worth griping about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.160
the overall consensus for "Black Adam" seems to&nbsp;
be that it's a possible scale-tipper for DC's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.020
Extended Universe following Marvel's recent&nbsp;
missteps with critically-lukewarm films like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.620
"Black Widow," "Eternals," "Doctor Strange&nbsp;
in the Multiverse of Madness," and "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.120
Love and Thunder." Some people have even wondered&nbsp;
if fans are getting tired of Marvel movies now in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.680
the wake of the conclusion to the decade-long&nbsp;
Infinity Saga. If the early reviews of "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.380
Adam" are true, then Johnson may not have been&nbsp;
ambitious enough when he said this sentiment.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:24.420
"The hierarchy of power in the&nbsp;
DC universe is about to change."

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.400
For many reviewers, DC's "Black Adam" isn't&nbsp;
just a breath of fresh air for the Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:34.800
superhero genre, but all of the DCEU as a&nbsp;
whole. Ben Rolph of DiscussingFilm tweeted:

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.220
"#BlackAdam is DC's most action-packed film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:44.100
to date. It's a non-stop thrill ride that&nbsp;
is all about spectacle, and it knows it."

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.000
He also added,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.400
"[Dwayne Johnson] is a perfect Black&nbsp;
Adam, plus Pierce Brosnan is a standout."

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.320
Content creator and entertainment journalist Matt&nbsp;
Ramos hasn't seen "Black Adam" yet, but he fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.960
expects the film to help shift the tide for Warner&nbsp;
Bros. and DC Films. On October 12, Ramos tweeted:

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.720
"If #BlackAdam is as GREAT as the reviews&nbsp;
say, DC might've slammed Marvel this year."

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.500
In a separate tweet, which came later&nbsp;
in the night as more and more reviews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.820
for "Black Adam" rolled in, Ramos&nbsp;
declared, quote, "DC is back."

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:20.160
While the Marvel vs. DC rivalry may be fun for&nbsp;
fans and critics, it's something that the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.440
stars themselves apparently don't pay much mind to&nbsp;
— or at least that's how Dwayne Johnson sees it.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.760
"I kneel before no one."

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.400
In an October 12 interview at&nbsp;
the New York City premiere of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.320
"Black Adam," he told the Associated Press:

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:37.140
"Do I think we are going to take any kind of bite&nbsp;
out of Marvel? That answer is unequivocally no."

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.160
Johnson added,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:44.460
"We don't want to be Marvel. We want to be DC. And&nbsp;
how we do things. So that's what I want. I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:50.100
want to take a bite of that apple. I want to grab&nbsp;
a new apple. And I want to create from there."

